35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"It seems we have a problem. Our in-house developers are busy until the third quarter, and the coordination group is understaffed, with people still writing logs by hand. I'm worried about who will do the extra work.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is concerning, Minato. I've found that network coverage at customer plants is very unreliable, with frequent outages and slow device approval. We must be cautious about any proposal that relies on constant connectivity or quick site access.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"I have found that our capital budget is frozen, though we have some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses will only increase our costs as we scale, whereas fixed-fee work remains stable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's a bit of a wake-up call, isn't it? I found that tools requiring daily input from everyone usually fail, while narrow, specialized tools survive. Also, most cross-unit efforts just collapse without a clear owner.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's heartbreaking to see how much time is wasted. I found that staff lose nearly an hour daily just copying existing records, and we've had eleven misrouted deliveries because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, that sounds so tiring for the staff. If we can find a way to stop that copying and the delivery mistakes, it would help a lot, but I'm still worried about who will manage it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, your concern is valid. Given that our developers are unavailable until the third quarter and the interfaces are undocumented, any complex new build would likely place an unfair burden on the remaining staff.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, that is a critical point. If we cannot rely on internal developers and our capital budget is frozen, we must prioritize solutions that are cost-stable and do not require heavy initial investment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. And let's not forget that if we pick something that requires everyone to change their daily habits, it'll probably be dead by next year. We need something specialized and sustainable, not a grand ambition.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree with May. We should look for a solution that solves these concrete, daily frustrations—like the record copying and address errors—without demanding an impossible amount of effort from an already exhausted staff.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I agree with everyone. We need a solution that helps the staff without adding more to their plate, especially since the coordination group is already struggling so much. I hope the candidates fit these needs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"We must be particularly wary of any proposal that assumes seamless field operations. If a tool requires a stable connection at customer plants to function, it will likely fail and cause more frustration than it solves.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree. We must avoid any project that creates a recurring financial burden we cannot predict. A fixed-fee approach is far safer than per-head licensing, especially if we are scaling across multiple departments.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"It sounds like we're all on the same page. We need something that doesn't require a miracle from our developers, doesn't bankrupt us via licenses, and actually survives the first year. Let's see if any of these candidates are actually realistic.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,I hope we can find a candidate that addresses those repetitive errors and wasted hours. It would be wonderful to give the staff some of their time back without adding new stresses to their day.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we have a very clear set of criteria now. We need something that is affordable, doesn't rely on our busy developers, works offline, and solves real problems without adding more work. I'm ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We have a clear understanding of the risks. Let us see if any of the proposals are grounded in these realities rather than optimistic assumptions. I am ready to review the candidates.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I agree. We have a solid framework for evaluation. Let us see if any of the proposals are fiscally responsible and operationally viable. I am ready to see the candidates.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I'm ready too. Let's just hope we have at least one option that isn't a total fantasy. I'll be looking for something that actually has a chance of surviving the first year.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Let's hope we find a proposal that truly supports our people and fixes those daily frustrations. I am ready to see the candidates and find the best way to help.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
