60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Looking at these, Candidate C seems best. It fixes the address errors Midori found and the record copying, and it doesn't seem to need the developers as much as a new app would.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I must disagree with Candidate D; the network issues I found make a field app too risky. Candidate C is better, but we must ensure it doesn't require the daily input that May warned us about.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Candidate C is promising, but we must be careful. If it requires per-head licenses for every user across all units, it will be too expensive. A fixed-fee implementation would be much more sustainable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you're right. Candidate A is a disaster waiting to happen—it's exactly the kind of ""everyone does it daily"" tool that fails. Candidate C is the only one that feels specialized enough to actually survive.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. Candidate C directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the hours wasted on copying records. It solves real, daily pain for our staff without the risks associated with field connectivity or constant daily input.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I feel very happy that we all agree on Candidate C. It helps the people who are tired of copying records and fixes the delivery mistakes, which is the kindest choice for the staff.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is the most prudent choice. It avoids the connectivity pitfalls of Candidate D and the sustainability issues of Candidate A, while addressing the documented inefficiencies without requiring immediate, heavy developer intervention.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"I agree. As long as we implement it as a fixed-fee project rather than a per-head license model, it fits our current budget constraints and avoids future financial surprises. It is the most responsible path forward.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"It's rare we all agree so quickly, but it makes sense. Candidate C is a targeted fix for a specific mess, not a vague productivity dream. It's the only one that doesn't look like a total waste of time.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"It really feels like the right decision. By consolidating those supplier records, we can stop the frustration of misrouted deliveries and give our colleagues their time back. I'm glad we're choosing something that truly helps.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I will vote for Candidate C. It is the best way to help our colleagues and reduce their burden without making the coordination group even more stressed.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will also vote for Candidate C. It is the only option that aligns with our technical constraints and avoids the risks of unreliable field connectivity and unsustainable developer demands.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I will vote for Candidate C. It is the most fiscally sound option and addresses the operational inefficiencies we've identified without risking an unpredictable recurring cost.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for Candidate C. It's the only one that doesn't look like a textbook example of a project that will be abandoned in six months. Let's actually fix something for once.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I will also vote for Candidate C. It is the most compassionate choice, as it directly removes the daily burdens and errors that frustrate our staff. I am happy we found a solution that truly supports them.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I am glad we could all agree on a way to help our coworkers. I will say ""Over"" now.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
